  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Amphicarpaea bracteata",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphicarpaea_bracteata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1368793555,
      "text": "Amphicarpaea bracteata is an annual to perennial vine in the legume family, native to woodland, thickets, and moist slopes in eastern North America. A. bracteata can be found in eastern North America, as well as further west into the Midwestern region, including Iowa, Indiana, Illinois, and Wisconsin."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Amphicarpaea bracteata",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphicarpaea_bracteata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 171582975,
      "text": "Amphicarpaea bracteata es una especie de planta trepadora anual o perenne perteneciente a la familia de las fabáceas, originaria de los bosques, matorrales y laderas húmedas del este de América del Norte y Asia oriental."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Amphicarpe bractéolée",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphicarpe_bract%C3%A9ol%C3%A9e",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 220254422,
      "text": "L'Amphicarpe bractéolée est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Fabaceae originaire du centre et de l’est de l’Amérique du Nord."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Amphicarpaea bracteata § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphicarpaea_bracteata#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1368793555,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "■ Biological studies\nA. bracteata has been used in botanical studies due to its reproductive plasticity and ability to produce diverse plant structures, such as flowers and seeds with varying reproductive functions and traits depending on its resources and environmental conditions. Some of the diverse structures studied include cleistogamous and chasmogamous flowers, and aerial and subterranean seeds and flowers.\n\n■ Agricultural and medicinal uses\n\nThe name 'hog-peanut\" comes from the grazing of plants and consumption of the subterranean seeds by hogs and other livestock.\nAmphicarpaea was used by indigenous groups, like the Cherokee and Iroquois people, as an antidiarrheal, gastric medication, and cathartic, as well as a treatment for snake bites and tuberculosis.\n\n■ Nitrogen-fixation\nLike other members of the Fabaceae family, Amphicarpaea house nitrogen-fixing bacteria which can fix atmospheric nitrogen that enters the soil. Nitrogen-fixation is a vital process for agriculture and can act as a natural fertilizer that promotes the production of vital proteins in plants, contributing to their growth.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Amphicarpe bractéolée § Utilisations",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amphicarpe_bract%C3%A9ol%C3%A9e#Utilisations",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 220254422,
        "heading": "Utilisations",
        "text": "■ Alimentaires\nL'Amphicarpe bractéolée peut être utilisée comme les autres légumineuses.\n\n■ Horticole\nL'Amphicarpe bractéolée est utilisé comme couvre-sol ornemental.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
